@flexiarg operator/ask-what-the-term-in-the-report-refers-to
@title Ask What A Term In The Agent's Report Refers To, And Say It Is New
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 2 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-lzfg2C turn-puWa5I
@parent operator/name-the-invented-component-and-say-it-should-not-exist
@context An agent's report uses a term the operator does not recognise, with a large count attached.

! conclusion: Say where the term is defined (file, record or spec), what the count counts, or that it was your own label.

  + IF:
    He asks what it is and says it is new to him.

  + HOWEVER:
    The agent may define the term fluently without saying where it came from.

  + THEN:
    Say where the term is defined (file, record or spec), what the count counts, or that it was your own label.

  + BECAUSE:
    The operator knows the design and can tell the term is not in it, so the source is the missing fact.
